{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582791962,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5784109001D13hHzBSlXoOcj","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d5782f91001G5h3qRWXQp6rhD","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-be55fa06aefabf77","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.codex/SYNC.md","limit":80},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.codex/SYNC.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Codex CLI — Runtime Sync Manifest\"\n3: description: \"How .codex derives from .skilled: the two generators that own agents and prompts, the installer that keeps the user-global hook file free of repo copies, and how to detect drift.\"\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Codex CLI Sync Manifest\n7: \n8: > The only fully **generated** runtime. `.codex/agents/` and `.codex/prompts/` are compiler output — never hand-edit them; edit the canonical source and re-run the generator.\n9: \n10: ---\n11: \n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: Codex differs from every sibling runtime in two ways.\n15: \n16: First, it cannot consume the shared trees directly: it needs TOML agents and a flat prompt namespace. So instead of symlinks, two generators transform `.skilled/` into Codex's dialect. Both own their output directory completely — they delete anything they did not generate.\n17: \n18: Second, Codex reads this repo's `.codex/hooks.json` itself once the checkout is trusted, so the user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json` must not carry copies of those entries: a copy registers each hook twice and Codex runs it twice per event. `install-codex-hooks.mjs` keeps the global file clean by removing repo-owned entries and orphans while preserving any third-party entries it finds there.\n19: \n20: Canonical for agents is `.skilled/agents/` (note: *not* `.claude/agents/`, which is what Cursor and Devin use — the two upstreams differ).\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. SURFACE INVENTORY\n25: \n26: | Surface | Mechanism | Source | Can it drift? |\n27: |---|---|---|---|\n28: | `agents/*.toml` | **generated** | `.skilled/agents/*.md` | Yes — `sync-agents.cjs --check` |\n29: | `prompts/*.md` (44) | **generated** pointer stubs | `.skilled/commands/**/*.md` | Yes — `sync-prompts.cjs --check` |\n30: | `hooks/*` (26 symlinks) | per-file symlinks | scattered `.skilled/**` | Yes — mirror generator |\n31: | `hooks.json` | **generated** | `hook-registry.json`, rendered by `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Yes, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs --check` reports it. Read by Codex from this checkout, never copied to `~/.codex/hooks.json` |\n32: | `config.toml` | **hand-authored** | — | MCP servers inlined here, unlike `.claude`/`.cursor` which use `mcp.json` |\n33: | `manual-testing-playbook/` | whole-dir symlink | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/manual-testing-playbook` | No |\n34: \n35: There is no `.codex/commands/` — prompts serve that role. There is no `.codex/skills/`.\n36: \n37: Each prompt is a ~750-byte stub that points at the canonical file rather than duplicating it:\n38: \n39: ```markdown\n40: <!-- Generated by sync-prompts.cjs from .skilled/commands/create/skill.md — do not edit by hand. -->\n41: # Codex entry: /create-skill\n42: … Read that file in full and follow it exactly …\n43: User request: $ARGUMENTS\n44: ```\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. WHEN TO SYNC\n49: \n50: - Any `.skilled/agents/*.md` changes → re-run `sync-agents.cjs`.\n51: - Any `.skilled/commands/**` file is added, renamed or deleted → re-run `sync-prompts.cjs`. Renames matter: a deleted canonical file leaves a stale prompt that points at nothing.\n52: - `.codex/hooks.json` changes → nothing to install, because Codex reads the file from the checkout. Run `install-codex-hooks.mjs --check` to confirm the user-global file holds no stale copy.\n53: - A hook is added or rebound → edit `hook-registry.json`, run `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` to render `hooks.json`, then run the mirror generator for the matching `hooks/` symlink.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 4. SYNC WORKFLOW\n58: \n59: ```bash\n60: # 1. Regenerate both owned trees (each deletes output it no longer expects)\n61: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n62: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n63: \n64: # 2. Render hooks.json from the shared hook registry, then refresh the hooks discovery mirror\n65: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\n66: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n67: \n68: # 3. Remove stale copies of repo hooks from the user-global Codex hook file\n69: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs          # backs up first; --dry-run to preview\n70: ```\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 5. FORMAT CONTRACT\n75: \n76: Agents are TOML with the body carried in a triple-quoted string:\n77: \n78: ```toml\n79: # Agent: review\n80: # Converted from: .skilled/agents/review.md\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.codex/SYNC.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Codex CLI — Runtime Sync Manifest\"\n3: description: \"How .codex derives from .skilled: the two generators that own agents and prompts, the installer that keeps the user-global hook file free of repo copies, and how to detect drift.\"\n4: ---\n5: \n6: # Codex CLI Sync Manifest\n7: \n8: > The only fully **generated** runtime. `.codex/agents/` and `.codex/prompts/` are compiler output — never hand-edit them; edit the canonical source and re-run the generator.\n9: \n10: ---\n11: \n12: ## 1. OVERVIEW\n13: \n14: Codex differs from every sibling runtime in two ways.\n15: \n16: First, it cannot consume the shared trees directly: it needs TOML agents and a flat prompt namespace. So instead of symlinks, two generators transform `.skilled/` into Codex's dialect. Both own their output directory completely — they delete anything they did not generate.\n17: \n18: Second, Codex reads this repo's `.codex/hooks.json` itself once the checkout is trusted, so the user-global `~/.codex/hooks.json` must not carry copies of those entries: a copy registers each hook twice and Codex runs it twice per event. `install-codex-hooks.mjs` keeps the global file clean by removing repo-owned entries and orphans while preserving any third-party entries it finds there.\n19: \n20: Canonical for agents is `.skilled/agents/` (note: *not* `.claude/agents/`, which is what Cursor and Devin use — the two upstreams differ).\n21: \n22: ---\n23: \n24: ## 2. SURFACE INVENTORY\n25: \n26: | Surface | Mechanism | Source | Can it drift? |\n27: |---|---|---|---|\n28: | `agents/*.toml` | **generated** | `.skilled/agents/*.md` | Yes — `sync-agents.cjs --check` |\n29: | `prompts/*.md` (44) | **generated** pointer stubs | `.skilled/commands/**/*.md` | Yes — `sync-prompts.cjs --check` |\n30: | `hooks/*` (26 symlinks) | per-file symlinks | scattered `.skilled/**` | Yes — mirror generator |\n31: | `hooks.json` | **generated** | `hook-registry.json`, rendered by `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` | Yes, `sync-hook-registrations.cjs --check` reports it. Read by Codex from this checkout, never copied to `~/.codex/hooks.json` |\n32: | `config.toml` | **hand-authored** | — | MCP servers inlined here, unlike `.claude`/`.cursor` which use `mcp.json` |\n33: | `manual-testing-playbook/` | whole-dir symlink | `.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-codex/manual-testing-playbook` | No |\n34: \n35: There is no `.codex/commands/` — prompts serve that role. There is no `.codex/skills/`.\n36: \n37: Each prompt is a ~750-byte stub that points at the canonical file rather than duplicating it:\n38: \n39: ```markdown\n40: <!-- Generated by sync-prompts.cjs from .skilled/commands/create/skill.md — do not edit by hand. -->\n41: # Codex entry: /create-skill\n42: … Read that file in full and follow it exactly …\n43: User request: $ARGUMENTS\n44: ```\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. WHEN TO SYNC\n49: \n50: - Any `.skilled/agents/*.md` changes → re-run `sync-agents.cjs`.\n51: - Any `.skilled/commands/**` file is added, renamed or deleted → re-run `sync-prompts.cjs`. Renames matter: a deleted canonical file leaves a stale prompt that points at nothing.\n52: - `.codex/hooks.json` changes → nothing to install, because Codex reads the file from the checkout. Run `install-codex-hooks.mjs --check` to confirm the user-global file holds no stale copy.\n53: - A hook is added or rebound → edit `hook-registry.json`, run `sync-hook-registrations.cjs` to render `hooks.json`, then run the mirror generator for the matching `hooks/` symlink.\n54: \n55: ---\n56: \n57: ## 4. SYNC WORKFLOW\n58: \n59: ```bash\n60: # 1. Regenerate both owned trees (each deletes output it no longer expects)\n61: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-agents.cjs\n62: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/codex/sync-prompts.cjs\n63: \n64: # 2. Render hooks.json from the shared hook registry, then refresh the hooks discovery mirror\n65: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-hook-registrations.cjs\n66: node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs\n67: \n68: # 3. Remove stale copies of repo hooks from the user-global Codex hook file\n69: node .skilled/bin/install-codex-hooks.mjs          # backs up first; --dry-run to preview\n70: ```\n71: \n72: ---\n73: \n74: ## 5. FORMAT CONTRACT\n75: \n76: Agents are TOML with the body carried in a triple-quoted string:\n77: \n78: ```toml\n79: # Agent: review\n80: # Converted from: .skilled/agents/review.md\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.codex/SYNC.md\", \"limit\": 80}"},"time":{"start":1794582790409,"end":1794582791962}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582791968,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5784380001yLlk5uW7cBWOO4","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d5782f91001G5h3qRWXQp6rhD","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-89f73271b858bce2","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md","offset":25,"limit":60},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md, lines 25-79\n25: \n26: - Use this when authoring a new slash command under `.skilled/commands/`.\n27: - Use this when modifying command frontmatter, execution paths, or command-owned assets.\n28: - Use this when adding `:auto` or `:confirm` behavior through YAML execution files.\n29: - Use this when changing command availability across OpenCode and Claude runtime paths.\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## 2. PRE-CHECKS\n34: \n35: - [ ] Read a YAML-router command such as `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` or `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`.\n36: - [ ] Read a contract-renderer command such as `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`, which delegates to `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`.\n37: - [ ] Confirm command frontmatter uses the live fields `argument-hint` and `allowed-tools` when the command needs arguments or tool permissions.\n38: - [ ] Confirm whether `:auto` needs PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS support in `argument-hint` and the presentation or compiled contract.\n39: - [ ] For YAML-router commands, verify real assets such as `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n40: - [ ] For contract-renderer commands, verify the rendered contract source such as `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown` and workflow assets such as `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n41: - [ ] Confirm command scope, required user inputs, dispatch targets, and file-write authority.\n42: - [ ] Classify the command's runtime scope, then run the mirror generator. `.claude/commands` is a real filtered tree of per-command symlinks, so OpenCode-only commands must be excluded deliberately.\n43: - [ ] Do not mirror commands into `.skilled/prompts/`; that path is not present in this workspace.\n44: - [ ] Confirm the command does not bypass skill-owned workflows for deep research, deep review, memory save, or spec folder writes.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. STEPS\n49: \n50: 1. Define the command trigger, supported suffixes, and expected arguments.\n51: 2. Choose the architecture.\n52:    - Contract-renderer: the command markdown is a small wrapper that invokes `render-command-contract.cjs` and lets the compiled contract own setup, routing, and workflow text.\n53:    - YAML-router: the command markdown owns mode selection and presentation-contract loading, then executes one workflow YAML asset.\n54: 3. Author command frontmatter with `description`, `argument-hint`, and `allowed-tools` when the command needs them.\n55: 4. For YAML-router commands, add or update presentation and workflow assets under the command asset directory.\n56: 5. For contract-renderer commands, keep the wrapper minimal and update the rendered contract source or deep-loop runtime assets instead of duplicating behavior in the wrapper.\n57: 6. Reference the owning skill and any agent dispatch contracts by exact path or command name.\n58: 7. Run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` for Claude parity; do not add manual command mirrors or `.skilled/prompts` entries.\n59: 8. Validate links, command examples, contract-renderer references, and YAML workflow references.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. POST-CHECKS\n64: \n65: - [ ] Run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` against the owning spec folder when the command change is part of a spec folder.\n66: - [ ] grep verification for command frontmatter: `rg -n \"^(description|argument-hint|allowed-tools):\" .skilled/commands/create/skill.md .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md .skilled/commands/deep/research.md`.\n67: - [ ] grep verification for YAML-router assets: `rg -n \"create_skill_(auto|confirm)\\\\.yaml|speckit_complete_(auto|confirm)\\\\.yaml|presentation\" .skilled/commands/create/skill.md .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`.\n68: - [ ] grep verification for contract-renderer commands: `rg -n \"render-command-contract\\\\.cjs|deep/research\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`.\n69: - [ ] Filtered parity check: `.claude/commands` is a real directory, each shared command is a symlink, excluded commands are absent, and `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` exits 0. `.skilled/prompts` should remain absent.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n74: \n75: - YAML-router examples: `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`\n76: - Contract-renderer example: `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`\n77: - Renderer: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`\n78: - Command parity path: generated per-command symlinks under `.claude/commands`\n79: - Verification recipes: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/universal-checklist.md`","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md, lines 25-79\n25: \n26: - Use this when authoring a new slash command under `.skilled/commands/`.\n27: - Use this when modifying command frontmatter, execution paths, or command-owned assets.\n28: - Use this when adding `:auto` or `:confirm` behavior through YAML execution files.\n29: - Use this when changing command availability across OpenCode and Claude runtime paths.\n30: \n31: ---\n32: \n33: ## 2. PRE-CHECKS\n34: \n35: - [ ] Read a YAML-router command such as `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md` or `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`.\n36: - [ ] Read a contract-renderer command such as `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`, which delegates to `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`.\n37: - [ ] Confirm command frontmatter uses the live fields `argument-hint` and `allowed-tools` when the command needs arguments or tool permissions.\n38: - [ ] Confirm whether `:auto` needs PRE-BOUND SETUP ANSWERS support in `argument-hint` and the presentation or compiled contract.\n39: - [ ] For YAML-router commands, verify real assets such as `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-auto.yaml`, `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-confirm.yaml`, and `.skilled/commands/create/assets/create-skill-presentation.txt`.\n40: - [ ] For contract-renderer commands, verify the rendered contract source such as `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/compiled/deep-research.contract.markdown` and workflow assets such as `.skilled/commands/deep/assets/deep-research-auto.yaml`.\n41: - [ ] Confirm command scope, required user inputs, dispatch targets, and file-write authority.\n42: - [ ] Classify the command's runtime scope, then run the mirror generator. `.claude/commands` is a real filtered tree of per-command symlinks, so OpenCode-only commands must be excluded deliberately.\n43: - [ ] Do not mirror commands into `.skilled/prompts/`; that path is not present in this workspace.\n44: - [ ] Confirm the command does not bypass skill-owned workflows for deep research, deep review, memory save, or spec folder writes.\n45: \n46: ---\n47: \n48: ## 3. STEPS\n49: \n50: 1. Define the command trigger, supported suffixes, and expected arguments.\n51: 2. Choose the architecture.\n52:    - Contract-renderer: the command markdown is a small wrapper that invokes `render-command-contract.cjs` and lets the compiled contract own setup, routing, and workflow text.\n53:    - YAML-router: the command markdown owns mode selection and presentation-contract loading, then executes one workflow YAML asset.\n54: 3. Author command frontmatter with `description`, `argument-hint`, and `allowed-tools` when the command needs them.\n55: 4. For YAML-router commands, add or update presentation and workflow assets under the command asset directory.\n56: 5. For contract-renderer commands, keep the wrapper minimal and update the rendered contract source or deep-loop runtime assets instead of duplicating behavior in the wrapper.\n57: 6. Reference the owning skill and any agent dispatch contracts by exact path or command name.\n58: 7. Run `node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/runtime-mirrors/sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs` for Claude parity; do not add manual command mirrors or `.skilled/prompts` entries.\n59: 8. Validate links, command examples, contract-renderer references, and YAML workflow references.\n60: \n61: ---\n62: \n63: ## 4. POST-CHECKS\n64: \n65: - [ ] Run `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh` against the owning spec folder when the command change is part of a spec folder.\n66: - [ ] grep verification for command frontmatter: `rg -n \"^(description|argument-hint|allowed-tools):\" .skilled/commands/create/skill.md .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md .skilled/commands/deep/research.md`.\n67: - [ ] grep verification for YAML-router assets: `rg -n \"create_skill_(auto|confirm)\\\\.yaml|speckit_complete_(auto|confirm)\\\\.yaml|presentation\" .skilled/commands/create/skill.md .skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`.\n68: - [ ] grep verification for contract-renderer commands: `rg -n \"render-command-contract\\\\.cjs|deep/research\" .skilled/commands/deep/research.md .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`.\n69: - [ ] Filtered parity check: `.claude/commands` is a real directory, each shared command is a symlink, excluded commands are absent, and `sync-runtime-mirrors.cjs --check` exits 0. `.skilled/prompts` should remain absent.\n70: \n71: ---\n72: \n73: ## 5. RELATED RESOURCES\n74: \n75: - YAML-router examples: `.skilled/commands/create/skill.md`, `.skilled/commands/speckit/complete.md`\n76: - Contract-renderer example: `.skilled/commands/deep/research.md`\n77: - Renderer: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/runtime/scripts/render-command-contract.cjs`\n78: - Command parity path: generated per-command symlinks under `.claude/commands`\n79: - Verification recipes: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/universal-checklist.md`"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md\", \"offset\": 25, \"limit\": 60}"},"time":{"start":1794582791040,"end":1794582791968}}}}
