{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582796805,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785570001SLoTKi6sC6Xi9a","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d5784e9c001wofDjFk3XNCZ35","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8075a38c5c0c9151","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md","offset":1195,"limit":25},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md, lines 1195-1219\n1195: \n1196: Writes the handoff note and prepares the relaunch record. Under the wrapper the runtime then restarts in the same terminal and the new session claims the note. Outside the wrapper it prints the command that continues the work in a new session.\n1197: \n1198: It is the only trigger on Cursor and Devin. Claude Code, Codex, Pi and OpenCode reach the same steps on their own near the context limit. It refuses while in-session handover is off, see [In-Session Handover](#in-session-handover).\n1199: \n1200: **`/speckit:search`**\n1201: \n1202: Two lexical lanes over spec docs and skill docs: trigger-index lookup with `--triggers`, which on a zero-hit also checks spec docs the index does not list yet, ripgrep recipes otherwise. `--paths` and `--count` pick the recipe, and `--packet <specFolder>` narrows the search roots. A phrase nobody wrote is a clean no-hit, never a nearest guess.\n1203: \n1204: &nbsp;\n1205: \n1206: #### CREATE\n1207: \n1208: **`/create:skill`** - unified skill creation and update workflow\n1209: \n1210: Creates `SKILL.md` with 8-section structure, `README.md`, references and assets directories. It registers nothing: discovery reads `graph-metadata.json`, and the advisor refresh stays with the operator. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1211: \n1212: **`/create:skill-parent`** - parent skill with nested modes\n1213: \n1214: Scaffolds a parent skill with nested mode packets: one hub identity plus a `mode-registry.json` source of truth the modes project from. It generates the routing-only `SKILL.md`, a single hub `graph-metadata.json`, N mode packets and a non-discoverable `shared/`. It is the reusable pattern behind `system-deep-loop`. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1215: \n1216: **`/create:agent`** - new agent definitions\n1217: \n1218: Scaffolds a new agent definition with proper frontmatter, behavioral rules and tool permissions. It creates the source-of-truth file in `.skilled/agents/` and the Claude Code mirror. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1219: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1220]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md, lines 1195-1219\n1195: \n1196: Writes the handoff note and prepares the relaunch record. Under the wrapper the runtime then restarts in the same terminal and the new session claims the note. Outside the wrapper it prints the command that continues the work in a new session.\n1197: \n1198: It is the only trigger on Cursor and Devin. Claude Code, Codex, Pi and OpenCode reach the same steps on their own near the context limit. It refuses while in-session handover is off, see [In-Session Handover](#in-session-handover).\n1199: \n1200: **`/speckit:search`**\n1201: \n1202: Two lexical lanes over spec docs and skill docs: trigger-index lookup with `--triggers`, which on a zero-hit also checks spec docs the index does not list yet, ripgrep recipes otherwise. `--paths` and `--count` pick the recipe, and `--packet <specFolder>` narrows the search roots. A phrase nobody wrote is a clean no-hit, never a nearest guess.\n1203: \n1204: &nbsp;\n1205: \n1206: #### CREATE\n1207: \n1208: **`/create:skill`** - unified skill creation and update workflow\n1209: \n1210: Creates `SKILL.md` with 8-section structure, `README.md`, references and assets directories. It registers nothing: discovery reads `graph-metadata.json`, and the advisor refresh stays with the operator. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1211: \n1212: **`/create:skill-parent`** - parent skill with nested modes\n1213: \n1214: Scaffolds a parent skill with nested mode packets: one hub identity plus a `mode-registry.json` source of truth the modes project from. It generates the routing-only `SKILL.md`, a single hub `graph-metadata.json`, N mode packets and a non-discoverable `shared/`. It is the reusable pattern behind `system-deep-loop`. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1215: \n1216: **`/create:agent`** - new agent definitions\n1217: \n1218: Scaffolds a new agent definition with proper frontmatter, behavioral rules and tool permissions. It creates the source-of-truth file in `.skilled/agents/` and the Claude Code mirror. Modes: `:auto`, `:confirm`.\n1219: \n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1220]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md\", \"offset\": 1195, \"limit\": 25}"},"time":{"start":1794582795632,"end":1794582796805}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582796810,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785582001qHJKlZJEoFUJW4","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d5784e9c001wofDjFk3XNCZ35","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-81545e09baa98ec1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md","offset":1680,"limit":22},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md, lines 1680-1701\n1680: \n1681: By default the runtime's own auto-compaction takes over, as it always did. In-session handover, which ships off, can hand the work to a fresh session instead, see [In-Session Handover](#in-session-handover).\n1682: \n1683: &nbsp;\n1684: \n1685: **Q: Can I use this framework without the continuity features?**\n1686: \n1687: Yes. The Spec Kit documentation workflow (Gate 3, spec folders, templates) works whether or not you ever run `/speckit:save`. You lose cross-session recovery, but structured documentation, agent routing and skill loading all still work.\n1688: \n1689: &nbsp;\n1690: \n1691: **Q: How can I add a new skill to the framework?**\n1692: \n1693: Use `/create:skill` to scaffold the skill structure. The command creates the `SKILL.md`, references and assets directories following the `sk-doc` template. Discovery reads its `SKILL.md` frontmatter and `graph-metadata.json`, so no registration step follows. Adding a row to `.skilled/skills/README.txt` keeps the catalog complete for human readers.\n1694: \n1695: &nbsp;\n1696: \n1697: **Q: What does \"local-first\" mean for continuity?**\n1698: \n1699: Everything is a file in your own repository. Continuity lives in the spec folder, and the trigger index is a committed JSON file. Retrieval is ripgrep over the working tree. No session data, code or context leaves the machine.\n1700: \n1701: &nbsp;\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1702]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md, lines 1680-1701\n1680: \n1681: By default the runtime's own auto-compaction takes over, as it always did. In-session handover, which ships off, can hand the work to a fresh session instead, see [In-Session Handover](#in-session-handover).\n1682: \n1683: &nbsp;\n1684: \n1685: **Q: Can I use this framework without the continuity features?**\n1686: \n1687: Yes. The Spec Kit documentation workflow (Gate 3, spec folders, templates) works whether or not you ever run `/speckit:save`. You lose cross-session recovery, but structured documentation, agent routing and skill loading all still work.\n1688: \n1689: &nbsp;\n1690: \n1691: **Q: How can I add a new skill to the framework?**\n1692: \n1693: Use `/create:skill` to scaffold the skill structure. The command creates the `SKILL.md`, references and assets directories following the `sk-doc` template. Discovery reads its `SKILL.md` frontmatter and `graph-metadata.json`, so no registration step follows. Adding a row to `.skilled/skills/README.txt` keeps the catalog complete for human readers.\n1694: \n1695: &nbsp;\n1696: \n1697: **Q: What does \"local-first\" mean for continuity?**\n1698: \n1699: Everything is a file in your own repository. Continuity lives in the spec folder, and the trigger index is a committed JSON file. Retrieval is ripgrep over the working tree. No session data, code or context leaves the machine.\n1700: \n1701: &nbsp;\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 1702]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/README.md\", \"offset\": 1680, \"limit\": 22}"},"time":{"start":1794582795650,"end":1794582796810}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794582796815,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"partID":"prt_1d5785817001fbbbln98O5MbpB","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d5784e9c001wofDjFk3XNCZ35","type":"tool","id":"chatcmpl-tool-acc389cf012f6a2f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/CONTRIBUTING.md","offset":188,"limit":18},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/CONTRIBUTING.md, lines 188-205\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: ## 6. 💡 WHAT TO CONTRIBUTE\n192: \n193: | Priority | Area | Description |\n194: |----------|------|-------------|\n195: | **High** | Bug fixes | With clear reproduction steps |\n196: | **High** | Performance | Improvements with benchmarks |\n197: | **High** | Documentation | Improvements and clarifications |\n198: | **Medium** | New skills | Scaffold with `/create:skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with nested modes |\n199: | **Medium** | Commands and agents | Scaffold with `/create:command` and `/create:agent` |\n200: | **Medium** | Tests | Test coverage |\n201: | **Always** | Typo fixes | Quick corrections welcome |\n202: | **Always** | Code clarity | Readability improvements |\n203: | **Always** | Translation | Convert non-English content to English |\n204: \n205: ---\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 206]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/CONTRIBUTING.md, lines 188-205\n188: \n189: ---\n190: \n191: ## 6. 💡 WHAT TO CONTRIBUTE\n192: \n193: | Priority | Area | Description |\n194: |----------|------|-------------|\n195: | **High** | Bug fixes | With clear reproduction steps |\n196: | **High** | Performance | Improvements with benchmarks |\n197: | **High** | Documentation | Improvements and clarifications |\n198: | **Medium** | New skills | Scaffold with `/create:skill`, or `/create:skill-parent` for a skill with nested modes |\n199: | **Medium** | Commands and agents | Scaffold with `/create:command` and `/create:agent` |\n200: | **Medium** | Tests | Test coverage |\n201: | **Always** | Typo fixes | Quick corrections welcome |\n202: | **Always** | Code clarity | Readability improvements |\n203: | **Always** | Translation | Convert non-English content to English |\n204: \n205: ---\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 206]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/CONTRIBUTING.md\", \"offset\": 188, \"limit\": 18}"},"time":{"start":1794582796311,"end":1794582796815}}}}
