eep-loop`.\nREADME.md:1301:| `/doctor:sk-skill` | `check`, `convert` | `check` | `convert` |\nREADME.md:1355:**`/doctor:sk-skill [check|convert] [<name-or-path>] [--json] [--into-hub <hub>] [--dry-run]`** - how far a skill is from the Skilled format, and the conversion that closes the gap\nREADME.md:1358:- `convert` prints a plan for a plain agent skill or an older Skilled one and writes only after your yes. It backs each file it overwrites up under `.skilled/skills/.state/doctor-sk-skill/<name>/` first, and stops when the parsed router would change. `--dry-run` ends after the plan. Three follow-ups are asked as their own question: a plain skill's intent phrases, at least eight of them, a description past 130 characters, and a skill with no `allowed-tools` field, whose question offers the list the plan proposes. A hub candidate is refused with `/create:skill-parent` named\nREADME.md:1557:- **Add your own surface** with `/create:skill-parent update --surfaces <name>`, which scaffolds and registers it ahead of the Skilled surface\nREADME.md:1693:Use `/create:sk-skill` to scaffold the skill structure. The command creates the `SKILL.md`, references and assets directories following the `sk-doc` template. Discovery reads its `SKILL.md` frontmatter and `graph-metadata.json`, so no registration step follows. Adding a row to `.skilled/skills/README.txt` keeps the catalog complete for human readers.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".codex/SYNC.md:40:<!-- Generated by sync-prompts.cjs from .skilled/commands/create/sk-skill.md — do not edit by hand. -->\n.codex/SYNC.md:41:# Codex entry: /create-sk-skill\n.claude/agents/markdown.md:39:- `/create:sk-skill`\n.claude/agents/markdown.md:44:- `/create:skill-parent`\n.claude/agents/markdown.md:182:| `/create:sk-skill`      | New skill `SKILL.md` or doc-only skill resource         | `.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/assets/skill/skill-md-