{"type":"text","timestamp":1794583178277,"sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","part":{"id":"prt_1d57e1f3c001176Jsx4ottlDKv","sessionID":"ses_e2a8827d1ffeTImD0J7JngRHUY","messageID":"msg_1d57dfc8c001rqa8sU608tU692","type":"text","text":"T009's six-file rename is written and the old-name scan is clean. `AMSC` still fails on the two generated agent mirrors that T016 owns.\n\nFiles changed:\n\n- `README.md`\n- `CONTRIBUTING.md`\n- `.skilled/agents/markdown.md`\n- `.claude/agents/markdown.md`\n- `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skills/...` corrected path: `.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-skilled/assets/checklists/command-authoring.md`\n- `.codex/SYNC.md`\n\nScoped diff is 15 insertions and 15 deletions across those six files, all rename lines.\n\nVerify output:\n\n```\n--- OLD over the six files ---\nOLD exit=1\n```\n\n`rg` exit 1 means no matches, so `OLD` printed nothing as required.\n\n```\n--- AMSC ---\nDRIFT  markdown [codex] missing=[\"sk-skill\"] unexpected=[]\nDRIFT  markdown [pi] missing=[\"sk-skill\"] unexpected=[]\nBLOCKED: 1 agent(s) have out-of-sync runtime mirrors: markdown\nAMSC exit=1\n```\n\nThe two failing files are `.codex/agents/markdown.toml` and `.pi/agents/markdown.md`. Both still carry `/create:skill`. They are generated output. The task rules say a generated file is written only by its generator, and no worker runs a generator that writes a runtime tree. T016 regenerates `.codex/agents`, `.pi/agents` and `.dsh/agents`.\n\nI did not run those generators, so I did not touch any file outside the six. There is no in-scope fix for the `AMSC` failure. I did not tick or edit `tasks.md`.\n\nNext: run T016, then re-run `node .skilled/bin/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` to close T009's second verify.","time":{"start":1794583174972,"end":1794583178277}}}
